{
  "id": "great-commission-05",
  "checkpoint": 5,
  "title": "Discipleship and Practical Steps",
  "summary": "Paul orienta seu novo irmão na fé sobre os passos práticos do discipulado: leitura diária das escrituras, vida devocional, mentoria e perseverança rumo à maturidade espiritual.",
  "audio_url": "/audios/great-commission-05.mp3",
  "word_count_target": 140,
  "story_en": "Over a warm meal, Paul explains that salvation is the beginning of a lifelong journey of discipleship. “Growing in faith requires daily spiritual nourishment,” Paul shares warmly.\n\nHe gives the young man a study journal and recommends establishing a consistent devotional routine. He encourages him to read the sacred scripture every morning, allowing God’s truth to guide his thoughts and decisions.\n\n“Christian maturity does not happen overnight,” Paul teaches. “It is developed through patient perseverance, prayer, and honest mentorship.”\n\nPaul commits to meeting with him weekly to answer questions, pray together, and offer guidance through life's challenges.\n\nWith a grateful heart and clear direction, the young disciple stands up. No longer lost or weighed down by guilt, he takes his first firm steps in a transformed life of faith and purpose.",
